{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0143mwc54bx1XaPEDE3urf8M","type":"tool_result","content":"candidates:\nsrc/lib/audio/__tests__/renderer-multiband.test.ts\nsrc/lib/audio/dsp/multiband.ts\nsrc/lib/audio/dsp/__tests__/multiband-parity.test.ts\nsrc/lib/audio/dsp/__tests__/parametric-eq-parity.test.ts\n=== find parity tests ===\nrenderer-bypass-parity.test.ts\n=== show commit afa8da4 files ===\ncommit afa8da4b64ce3b2658a2963910988fcdf4813aaf\nAuthor: Yosef Gamble <yegamble@gmail.com>\nDate:   Tue Jun 30 14:39:15 2026 -0400\n\n    test(dsp): numerical multiband worklet<->DSP parity (export == preview)\n    \n    The multiband parity test was source-inspection only. Add a numerical layer: load the worklet in a vm sandbox (EnvelopeScheduler absent → static params, no smoothing), drive it block-by-block, and assert its output equals MultibandCompressorDSP.processStereo to < 1e-6 across two configs (low-band stereo compression; all-bands incl. M/S). Proves the real-time worklet and the offline export DSP are sample-equivalent.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n .../audio/dsp/__tests__/multiband-parity.test.ts   | 224 ++++++++++++++++++++-\n 1 file changed, 221 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"243c3f7c-ee0e-426f-a231-33e2ba1d8e5c","uuid":"8aab55cd-f8d0-457c-8653-ec72ac16e5bc","timestamp":"2026-07-01T04:16:17.240Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"candidates:\nsrc/lib/audio/__tests__/renderer-multiband.test.ts\nsrc/lib/audio/dsp/multiband.ts\nsrc/lib/audio/dsp/__tests__/multiband-parity.test.ts\nsrc/lib/audio/dsp/__tests__/parametric-eq-parity.test.ts\n=== find parity tests ===\nrenderer-bypass-parity.test.ts\n=== show commit afa8da4 files ===\ncommit afa8da4b64ce3b2658a2963910988fcdf4813aaf\nAuthor: Yosef Gamble <yegamble@gmail.com>\nDate:   Tue Jun 30 14:39:15 2026 -0400\n\n    test(dsp): numerical multiband worklet<->DSP parity (export == preview)\n    \n    The multiband parity test was source-inspection only. Add a numerical layer: load the worklet in a vm sandbox (EnvelopeScheduler absent → static params, no smoothing), drive it block-by-block, and assert its output equals MultibandCompressorDSP.processStereo to < 1e-6 across two configs (low-band stereo compression; all-bands incl. M/S). Proves the real-time worklet and the offline export DSP are sample-equivalent.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n .../audio/dsp/__tests__/multiband-parity.test.ts   | 224 ++++++++++++++++++++-\n 1 file changed, 221 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
